# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Dependencies
- Added `@vercel/analytics@^1.6.1` to the project dependencies
- Used npm for installation (with --legacy-peer-deps due to peer dependency conflicts)
- Reinstalled with yarn to properly update the yarn.lock file

### 2. Modified Files

**app/layout.tsx**
- Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the ThemeProvider closing tag
- Placement ensures analytics tracking works correctly while maintaining existing app structure

**package.json**
- Added `@vercel/analytics` to dependencies section

**yarn.lock**
- Updated lockfile to reflect new dependency and its transitive dependencies

## Implementation Details

This is an App Router project (Next.js 15.0.0), so the Analytics component was added to the root layout file at `app/layout.tsx`. The component is placed at the end of the body tag, which is the recommended position for optimal performance and tracking accuracy.

The Analytics component will automatically:
- Track page views
- Monitor Web Vitals (CLS, FID, LCP, FCP, TTFB)
- Send analytics data to Vercel when deployed

## Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully (`yarn build`)
- ✅ No TypeScript errors
- ✅ All dependencies properly installed
- ✅ Lockfile updated correctly

## Notes

- The project uses yarn as its package manager (yarn.lock present)
- The Analytics component is lightweight and won't impact page load performance
- Analytics data will only be collected when the application is deployed to Vercel
- No additional configuration is required for basic analytics tracking
